ions and testing prerequisites at 6.4–6.8, then compare each prerequisite with the explicit and transitive dependsOn edges.","fixability":"assisted","proposedFix":{"rationale":"The evidence does not identify the target dependency graph, so neither a missing edge nor an exact artifact correction can be safely derived.","options":["Re-run scoped probes and anchor reads against the target artifact to verify dependency completeness.","Qualify the completeness claim as unverified pending an audit of later-story testing prerequisites."]}},{"claimId":"p38","ref":"S006:FR001","kind":"ordering","severity":"LOW","premise":"The acli command inventory and output evidence must be recorded before Jira tool families are designed.","evidence":"docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/DEF.md:62 explicitly requires checking and recording acli's command list and output before designing Jira tool families, with each family citing that evidence. DEF.md:241 (item a2) reiterates recording subcommands and output for transitions, comments, assignment and projects, plus missing-install versus missing-sign-in behavior, before Jira story design. These matches confirm the prescribed ordering.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual","proposedFix":{"rationale":"The evidence directly confirms the ordering requirement; no correction is needed."}},{"claimId":"p39","ref":"6.8/ac5","kind":"cross-artifact","severity":"MED","premise":"Stories s4 and s8 together are required to cover the recorded git command inventory, with exclusions limited to those accepted by the user.","evidence":"The supplied grep for git coverage, inventory, or exclusions returned 0 matches. No artifact reads establish the recorded inventory, s4/s8 coverage, or user-accepted exclusions, so the premise is unverifiable.","action":"Provide the recorded git command inventory, the s4 and s8 coverage mappings, and evidence of user-accepted exclusions for comparison.","fixability":"assisted","proposedFix